---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Navbar from '../components/Navbar.jsx';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.jsx';

const effective = 'August 5, 2026';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy Policy — RevFactor"
  description="How RevFactor collects, uses, stores, and protects information from short-term rental hosts who visit revfactor.io, subscribe to The Rev Journal, or book a Discovery Call."
  noindex={false}
>
  <Navbar client:load />

  <main class="bg-[#DDDAD3] pt-32 pb-24">
    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-6 md:px-10">
      <p class="font-bold uppercase text-[9px] tracking-[3px] text-[#5D6D59] mb-4">Legal</p>
      <h1 class="text-[#3F261F] mb-3" style="font-family:'Cormorant Garamond',Georgia,serif; font-weight:400; font-size:clamp(36px,5vw,56px); line-height:1.05; letter-spacing:0.5px;">Privacy Policy</h1>
      <p class="text-[14px] text-[#76574C] mb-12" style="font-family:'JetBrains Mono',monospace; letter-spacing:0.5px;">Effective {effective}</p>

      <div class="legal-prose text-[#3F261F]">
        <p>This Privacy Policy explains how REVFACTORIO LLC (&ldquo;RevFactor,&rdquo; &ldquo;we,&rdquo; &ldquo;us&rdquo;) collects, uses, and protects information when you visit <a href="https://www.revfactor.io">revfactor.io</a>, use our chat widget, subscribe to The Rev Journal, book a Discovery Call, or otherwise interact with our managed revenue management service for short-term rental hosts.</p>

        <h2>Information We Collect</h2>
        <p>We collect the following categories of information:</p>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Information you provide directly.</strong> Name, email address, phone number, property details, and any context you share when you book a Discovery Call, subscribe to The Rev Journal, complete a contact form, or correspond with us.</li>
          <li><strong>Chat and messaging data.</strong> When you use our LeadConnector chat widget, LeadConnector processes the contact details, messages, and consent choices you submit on our behalf. If you provide a mobile number, we also retain records of your messaging opt-in and opt-out choices.</li>
          <li><strong>Booking and consultation data.</strong> When you schedule a call through our Cal.com embedded booking, Cal.com processes the booking on our behalf and shares the booking record (name, email, scheduled time, your stated context) with RevFactor.</li>
          <li><strong>Usage and device data.</strong> Pages visited, referring URL, browser type, device type, approximate location (derived from IP address), and interaction events. We collect this automatically using PostHog, Google Analytics 4, and Umami Analytics.</li>
          <li><strong>Anti-fraud signals.</strong> We use Fraud Blocker to detect invalid clicks and bot traffic. Fraud Blocker may set cookies and collect device-fingerprint signals to distinguish humans from automated traffic.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>How We Use Information</h2>
        <p>RevFactor uses collected information to:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Operate, secure, and improve the revfactor.io website and our service.</li>
          <li>Respond to consultation requests and schedule discovery calls.</li>
          <li>Respond to chat inquiries and, only after separate express written consent, send promotional text messages.</li>
          <li>Send The Rev Journal newsletter, but only to subscribers who opt in. Every newsletter contains a one-click unsubscribe link.</li>
          <li>Measure marketing performance, optimize advertising, and detect invalid ad traffic.</li>
          <li>Comply with legal obligations and protect against fraud or abuse.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>Legal Bases (GDPR)</h2>
        <p>If you are in the European Economic Area or the United Kingdom, we rely on the following legal bases under Article 6 of the GDPR:</p>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Consent</strong> for newsletter subscriptions, marketing text messages, and non-essential cookies.</li>
          <li><strong>Legitimate interest</strong> for measuring site performance, detecting fraud, and responding to inquiries you initiated.</li>
          <li><strong>Contract performance</strong> for delivering services to clients who have engaged RevFactor.</li>
          <li><strong>Legal obligation</strong> when retention or disclosure is required by law.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>How We Share Information</h2>
        <p>RevFactor does not sell personal information. We share information only with service providers acting on our behalf, and only to the extent necessary to operate the service:</p>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Cal.com</strong> — calendar booking provider.</li>
          <li><strong>LeadConnector</strong> — embedded chat, messaging opt-in, consent records, and message delivery.</li>
          <li><strong>PostHog, Google Analytics 4, Google Ads, Umami</strong> — site analytics and conversion measurement.</li>
          <li><strong>Fraud Blocker</strong> — invalid-click detection.</li>
          <li><strong>Email service providers</strong> we use to send The Rev Journal (subscribers only).</li>
          <li><strong>Hosting and infrastructure</strong> providers (Vercel) that serve the website.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>We may also disclose information when required by law, to enforce our terms, or to protect the rights, safety, or property of RevFactor or others.</p>
        <p><strong>Mobile information will not be shared, sold, or transferred to third parties or affiliates for their own marketing or promotional purposes.</strong> We may share mobile information with service providers, such as LeadConnector, only as needed to operate our messaging program. Text-message opt-in data and consent records are not shared with third parties for marketing purposes.</p>

        <h2>Marketing Text Messages</h2>
        <p>If you voluntarily provide your mobile number through the chat widget and select the separate, optional marketing consent checkbox, you provide express written consent to receive recurring promotional and marketing text messages from REVFACTORIO LLC. Messages may include promotions, special offers, discounts, event announcements, service announcements, and other updates.</p>
        <p>Marketing consent is separate from any consent to receive transactional messages and is not a condition of purchase. Message frequency varies. Message and data rates may apply. Reply <strong>STOP</strong> to any message to unsubscribe or <strong>HELP</strong> for help. We honor opt-out requests and retain consent and opt-out records as needed to demonstrate compliance.</p>

        <h2>Cookies and Similar Technologies</h2>
        <p>RevFactor uses cookies and similar technologies to operate the site, remember preferences, measure performance, and prevent invalid traffic. See our <a href="/cookies/">Cookies Policy</a> for the full list and instructions on how to control them.</p>

        <h2>Data Retention</h2>
        <p>We retain personal information only as long as needed for the purposes described above, or as required by law. Newsletter records are retained until you unsubscribe. Messaging consent and opt-out records are retained as needed to operate the program and demonstrate compliance. Consultation records are retained for the duration of a working engagement plus a reasonable archival period. Analytics data is retained per the default retention of the underlying providers (PostHog, GA4, Umami).</p>

        <h2>Your Rights</h2>
        <p>Depending on your jurisdiction, you may have the right to access, correct, delete, port, or restrict processing of your personal information, and to object to certain uses. To exercise any of these rights, contact us at <a href="mailto:hello@revfactor.io">hello@revfactor.io</a>. We will respond within 30 days.</p>
        <p>California residents have specific rights under the California Consumer Privacy Act (CCPA), including the right to know what we collect, the right to delete personal information, and the right to opt out of any sale or sharing for cross-context behavioral advertising. RevFactor does not sell personal information.</p>

        <h2>Children's Privacy</h2>
        <p>RevFactor is a B2B service for STR hosts and is not directed to children under 16. We do not knowingly collect information from children.</p>

        <h2>Security</h2>
        <p>We use reasonable administrative, technical, and physical safeguards designed to protect personal information. No method of transmission or storage is 100% secure.</p>

        <h2>International Transfers</h2>
        <p>RevFactor operates from the United States. If you access the site from outside the U.S., your information may be transferred to, stored in, and processed in the U.S. and other countries where our service providers operate.</p>

        <h2>Changes to This Policy</h2>
        <p>We may update this Privacy Policy from time to time. Changes are effective when posted. Material changes will be flagged at the top of the page.</p>

        <h2>Contact</h2>
        <p>Questions about this Privacy Policy? Email <a href="mailto:hello@revfactor.io">hello@revfactor.io</a>.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </main>

  <Footer client:load />

  <style>
    .legal-prose { font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.7; color: #3F261F; }
    .legal-prose h2 {
      font-family: 'Cormorant Garamond', Georgia, serif;
      font-weight: 500;
      font-size: 26px;
      letter-spacing: 0.5px;
      color: #3F261F;
      margin: 36px 0 12px;
      padding-top: 24px;
      border-top: 1px solid rgba(118,87,76,0.15);
    }
    .legal-prose h2:first-of-type { border-top: none; padding-top: 0; }
    .legal-prose p { margin: 0 0 14px; color: #3F261F; }
    .legal-prose ul { padding-left: 22px; margin: 0 0 16px; }
    .legal-prose li { margin-bottom: 8px; }
    .legal-prose a { color: #13342D; text-decoration: underline; text-underline-offset: 3px; text-decoration-color: rgba(19,52,45,0.4); }
    .legal-prose a:hover { text-decoration-color: #13342D; }
    .legal-prose strong { color: #3F261F; font-weight: 600; }
  </style>
</BaseLayout>
